-### [Compact Box (CB)](17690-compact-box-cb.md)
-An extension of SnugBox that computes exact Gaussian-tile intersections during the duplicate-keys phase, emitting keys only for tiles the ellipse strictly overlaps, providing an additional speed-up over SnugBox alone.
+Compact Box (CB) is a preprocessing optimization for rasterization that reduces the number of Gaussian-tile pairs by tightening the effective support region of 2D Gaussians, eliminating unnecessary pairs where the Gaussian has negligible impact on pixels within a tile. It builds on SnugBox by introducing a scaling factor $\beta$ into the alpha blending equation, which further shrinks the 2D Gaussian footprint and intersection region with tiles compared to standard 3-sigma or precise tile-intersection methods.
+
+### Gaussian-aware intersection
+A technique to reduce invalid Gaussian evaluations by using tighter intersection tests between Gaussians and tiles/pixels [S4, unofficial]. AdR-Gaussian uses tight axis-aligned bounding boxes, while FlashGS refines Gaussian–tile intersection; both reduce associations, shrinking sorting input, traversal, and intermediate list traffic [S4, unofficial].
 
